# beta.6 (the owner's playtest): the prompts of a new game's first screens in one style (LAUNCHER_PROMPTS from the
# caller) -- the character select (Cross, Circle, L1, R1, Triangle), then the hero's naming screen (L1 / R1 to switch,
# Cross to select, Circle to erase), where v1.01 showed the PlayStation buttons whatever the style. Checked by
# tests/prompts_check.py (a run tagged pr-naming-<style>: the two screens' textures redrawn in that style, or none in
# PlayStation's). The flow is tests/scripts/intro.drive's; nothing is saved.
#! env PS3_VERBOSE=0 SHOT_EVERY=0 DUMP=1
#! secs 240
log TitleMovie 120          # the title's background movie is open
sleep 5
press START                 # "PRESS START BUTTON"
sleep 3
press START                 # -> main menu
change
sleep 3
press CROSS                 # NEW GAME
change
sleep 4
shot characters
press CROSS                 # the first character
change
sleep 2
press CROSS                 # "Is this okay?" YES
change
sleep 3
shot naming
press R1                    # the next page of letters: the screen's own switch, as its prompt says
sleep 1.5
shot naming-r1
